DESCRIPTION:Not everyone gets an A. In a traditional Chinese family\, the d
 aughter earns a law degree\; the son sells noodles from a cart. Stereotype 
 says: she's the golden child\, he's the disappointment. But another stereot
 ype says: sons are spoiled\, no matter what. In this family\, that one wins
 . The son is coddled. The daughter questioned. Then she brings home a forei
 gn fiancé with a "love" tattoo that actually says cancer. Almost A asks wh
 ich stereotypes are right\, wrong\, or almost right – through noodle cart
 s\, Princeton degrees\, and a family refusing one mold but happily squeezin
 g into another.\nMore info: https://comedyatlas.app/comedy-atlas/event/almo
 st-a/
